target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPrReportPostDefersAndReportsWhereTo'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    with -post the body goes to the PR, and stdout stays empty so a caller can tell "published" from "rendered". Printing both makes `looper pr-report --post > file` look like it still produces the report locally, and pipes a second copy into whatever Step 14 redirects.
--- old
	if !*post {
		_, err = io.WriteString(out, body)
		return err
	}
--- new
	_, err = io.WriteString(out, body)
	if !*post {
		return err
	}
